# family: predict
# bridge: A(laws + engine shadow zero + determinism floor)
# regime: bit-exact decisions
# instrument-first: 2be31477
# baseline: tests/unit/sim, tests/integration/sim, tests/unit/entity, tests/integration/lagcomp
# baseline-count: 543
# successor-form: matrix
#
# The unit is one predicting entity's engine: its tape, its journal, its
# command and ack lanes, its comparison and its recovery ladder. Nineteen of
# its twenty kernels are already native and certified, and that licensed
# nothing, because a certified kernel is a certified function and every case
# below is about an object with identity and memory.
#
# THE CROSSING IS AT THE SUITE, not the case. Every case of one suite names
# the same native successor, which is the representative cell of the law file
# that carries that suite's claims. `netw-ring0-cutover-campaign.md` section 1
# is the decision and states what the coarser grain buys and what it gives up.
#
# THE CAPABILITY SET the pool declares through `supports`:
#
#   schedule    TICK, FRAME, STEPPED
#   role        PREDICT, HOST_LOCAL, AUTHORITY, SIMULATE
#   correction  SNAP, REPLAY
#   restore     EXACT, EXTRAPOLATED
#   island      none, declared, joint
#   carry       none, declared
#   witness     none, declared
#
# SIMULATE requires a declared or joint island. Joint requires a re-runnable
# schedule, TICK or STEPPED. REPLAY requires EXACT restore. Carry and witness
# do not narrow support.
#
# WHAT STILL CARRIES. `tests/integration/lagcomp` holds the rewind, action and
# body-bound suites. Their old reason, "lagcomp has no native shell to cross
# into", is FALSIFIED: NetwLagCompCore is native and ZU-5 gave it the
# declaration filter, the armed port and the rewind verb. What is left is a
# real body in a physics space, which the treeless rig cannot give it. `tests/unit/core` holds
# the entity numbering, which is keyed by node.
#
